{title: 381 - Holy Sabbath Day of Rest}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Doctrines}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Eb]Holy Sabbath [Ab]day of [Eb]rest, By our Master richly [Bb]blest,
[Eb]God created [Ab]and di[Eb]vine, Set aside for [Bb]holy [Eb]time.
[Ab]Yes, the holy Sabbath [Eb]rest, By our God divinely [Bb]blest,
[Eb]It to us a sign shall [Ab]be [Eb]Throughout all e[Bb]terni[Eb]ty.

Refrain:
[Eb]Yes, [Ab]the [Eb]holy [Bb]Sabbath rest,
[Eb]By [Ab]our [Eb]God [Bb]divinely [Eb]blest,
[Ab]It to [Eb]us a [Bb]sign shall be
[Eb][Ab]Throughout [Eb][Bb]all [Eb]eternity.

Verse 2:
[Eb]Seek [Ab]not pleasures [Eb]of [Bb]this earth,
[Eb]With [Ab]its [Eb]folly, [Bb]noise, [Eb]and mirth,
[Ab]There are [Eb]better things [Bb]in store,
[Eb]Over [Ab]on [Eb]the [Bb]other [Eb]shore.

Verse 3:
[Eb]As [Ab]the [Eb]Sabbath [Bb]draweth on
[Eb]Friday [Ab]eve [Eb]at [Bb]set [Eb]of sun,
[Ab]Christian [Eb]household then [Bb]should meet,
[Eb]Sing [Ab]and [Eb]pray [Bb]at [Eb]Jesus'feet.

Verse 4:
[Eb]Asking [Ab]Him [Eb]for [Bb]saving grace,
[Eb]Also [Ab]vict'ry [Eb]in [Bb]the [Eb]race,
[Ab]And to [Eb]help us [Bb]by His pow'r,
[Eb]To [Ab]keep [Eb]holy [Bb]every [Eb]hour.
